    <bpmn:process id="W_W5170" name="W5170. EPR Recovery Credit Purchase Agreement (RCPA) Negotiation &amp; Trading" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly reconciliation (W5169) showing a recovery volume deficit
Frequency: Event-driven per deficit
Volume: ~1–2 credit purchase agreements annually
Owner: Director of Supply Chain / EPR Compliance Manager
Participants: EPR Credit Sellers (other companies, PROs), Legal Operations (VS-100), Treasury (VS-18)
Source: workflow W5170 — EPR Recovery Credit Purchase Agreement (RCPA) Negotiation &amp; Trading</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5170_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5170_Lane1" name="Director of Supply Chain">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5170_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5170_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5170_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5170_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5170_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5170_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5170_Start3" name="Quarterly reconciliation (W5169) showing a recovery volume deficit">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5170_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5170_Task4" name="Assess credit market: source excess recovery credits from companies exceeding…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Assess credit market: source excess recovery credits from companies exceeding their targets or specialized PRO pools.
Responsible (R): Director of Supply Chain / EPR Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): Director of Supply Chain / EPR Compliance Manager
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5170_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5170_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5170_Task5" name="Negotiate Recovery Credit Purchase Agreement (RCPA): define price per metric…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Negotiate Recovery Credit Purchase Agreement (RCPA): define price per metric ton, validation guarantees, and indemnification against NSWMC rejection.
Responsible (R): Director of Supply Chain / EPR Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): Director of Supply Chain / EPR Compliance Manager
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5170_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5170_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5170_Task6" name="Draft the RCPA contract and route for board approval (VS-36) if transaction…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Draft the RCPA contract and route for board approval (VS-36) if transaction value exceeds standard limits.
Responsible (R): Director of Supply Chain / EPR Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): Director of Supply Chain / EPR Compliance Manager
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5170_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5170_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5170_Task7" name="Release payment through Treasury and obtain the endorsed Plastic Recovery…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Release payment through Treasury and obtain the endorsed Plastic Recovery Certificates.
Responsible (R): Director of Supply Chain / EPR Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): Director of Supply Chain / EPR Compliance Manager
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5170_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5170_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5170_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5170_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5170_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-769 (ensure controlled execution — EPR Credit Trading, Compliance Auditing &amp; Annual Reporting (PA-179.3).) | - CTL-769: Seller certificates validated by legal before escrow payout; transactions board-authorized.
Owner: Director of Supply Chain / EPR Compliance Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
